From: Valery Petrov <valerypetrov@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 04:49:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the four tests the full CI suite found failing

The suite ran everything for the first time in several rounds and turned up
four failures, three of them the PR's own.

A missing shard table was reported as an unreachable replica rather than a
missing one: SHOW CREATE TABLE answers a name it cannot produce a DDL for
with CANNOT_GET_CREATE_TABLE_QUERY, not UNKNOWN_TABLE, so the probe's mapping
missed it and the write's refusal lost the diagnosis it is asserted to carry.

The stateless test of the new setting deadlocked under the randomized
settings the flaky and targeted jobs use. It had two views on one table, one
writing a Log table directly and one writing that same Log table again over a
Distributed table pointing back at this server, so the second waited on the
lock the first held for the whole statement. The nested hop only proved that
the requirement a table consumed does not travel a further Distributed hop,
which the view target of another type already proves without one.

Two assertions rested on premises that are not true. `error_code` lost its
`node` argument at one call site when it was factored out in the
simplification pass, which the integration suite has been failing on since.
And a cluster user granted nothing is not denied `system.tables`: every user
may read it and it filters the rows it shows, so the premise is that it shows
that user no row, not that it raises.

